From: 4reel contributors
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: cif: reject absent RV1106 scaler channels

RV1103/RV1106 implements only scaler channel 0. The TRM marks bits 31:8
of VICAP_SCL_CH_CTRL reserved and provides no CH1..3 DMA registers.
The generic driver exposes those nodes anyway; reject STREAMON instead of
silently succeeding with no frames.

---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/cif/cif-scale.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/cif/cif-scale.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/cif/cif-scale.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/cif/cif-scale.c
@@ -1287,6 +1287,9 @@ int rkcif_scale_start(struct rkcif_scale_vdev *scale_vdev)
 	struct rkcif_device *dev = scale_vdev->cifdev;
 	int ret = 0;
 
+	if (dev->chip_id == CHIP_RV1106_CIF && scale_vdev->ch != 0)
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
 	rkcif_scale_channel_init(scale_vdev);
 	if (dev->chip_id >= CHIP_RV1126B_CIF)
 		ret = rkcif_scale_channel_set_rv1126b(scale_vdev);
